{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Insert a profile into a world to find out where a schedule spends its time. Every schedule","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that runs on the world then records each system’s runs in it:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["var world = World()","world.resources.insert(SystemProfile())","world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 0, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","frame.run(on: &world)","","let timings = world.resources[SystemProfile.self].timings","print(timings.map(\\.name))","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gravity\", \"Movement\"]\"","print(timings.map(\\.runs))","\/\/ Prints \"[2, 2]\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" also holds the total, average, longest and latest time of the system’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"runs."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A run’s time covers the system’s own work, measured on a continuous clock: not its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conditions, nor the commands it queued, which apply after its wave. A system its conditions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"skip doesn’t run, so nothing is recorded for it. Systems in the same wave run at the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time, so their times can add up to more than the wave took. Insert a new profile to start"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile\/init()"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile\/timings"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Profiling","title":"Profiling"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"]]},"metadata":{"title":"SystemProfile","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemProfile"}],"externalID":"s:7Systems13SystemProfileV","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Profiling.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Systems\/Profiling.swift#L77"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemProfile"}],"modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure"},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Resource","doc:\/\/Systems\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Systems\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Resource":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/resource","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Resource"}],"title":"Resource","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Resource","abstract":[{"text":"A type that a world can hold a single value of, outside any entity.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Resource"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile/timings":{"kind":"symbol","title":"timings","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The timing of each system that has run, in the order the systems first ran."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile\/timings","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"timings"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems12SystemTimingV","text":"SystemTiming"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile\/timings","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SchedulingSystems":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Order the systems of a schedule, run them only when a condition holds, and find out how a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule runs them.","type":"text"}],"title":"Scheduling Systems","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulingsystems"},"doc://Systems/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/s8SendableP"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile/init()":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates an empty profile."}],"title":"init()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile\/init()","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile\/init()","rol